          "id": "l08",
          "speaker": "narrator",
          "text": "One kilo of fat needs nearly three kilos of oxygen, so your lungs do the heavy *lifting*.",
          "pauseAfterMs": 900
        },
        {
          "id": "l09",
          "speaker": "narrator",
          "text": "Your body pulls the oil apart and joins each piece to that *oxygen*.",
          "pauseAfterMs": 400
        },
        {
          "id": "l10",
          "speaker": "narrator",
          "text": "Only two leftovers come out: water, and carbon dioxide, the gas that fizzes in *soda*.",
          "pauseAfterMs": 400
        },
        {
          "id": "l11",
          "speaker": "narrator",
          "text": "That gas slips into your blood and rides it all the way up to your *lungs*.",
